{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NE5L6sSaPVEP7LH7wuFmEk","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd058-rm\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/rm: Remove Files or Directories\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  rm removes files and directories from the filesystem. The macOS BSD rm differs from\n6\t  GNU rm in interactive prompt formatting, --one-file-system behavior, and verbose output.\n7\t  The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (grm, installed by\n8\t  coreutils) on exit codes and observable file system state for all supported flag\n9\t  combinations, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\tgoals:\n12\t  - G1: Remove files and directories with configurable safety controls.\n13\t  - G2: Support recursive directory removal and interactive confirmation modes.\n14\t  - G3: Support force mode to suppress errors on non-existent files.\n15\t  - G4: Verify functional parity against grm via differential testing.\n16\t\n17\trequirements:\n18\t  R1:\n19\t    title: Basic file removal\n20\t    items:\n21\t      - R1.1:\n22\t          text: \"When given one or more FILE arguments, must remove each file using unlink(2).\"\n23\t      - R1.2:\n24\t          text: \"Without -r, must refuse to remove a directory and print an error to stderr.\"\n25\t      - R1.3:\n26\t          text: \"Must not remove '.' or '..' to prevent accidental directory tree destruction. Must print an error if either is specified.\"\n27\t      - R1.4:\n28\t          text: \"When a file cannot be removed (permission denied, in use), must print an error to stderr and continue with remaining files.\"\n29\t\n30\t  R2:\n31\t    title: Recursive removal and force mode\n32\t    items:\n33\t      - R2.1:\n34\t          text: \"-r or -R or --recursive must remove directories and their contents recursively.\"\n35\t      - R2.2:\n36\t          text: \"-f or --force must ignore non-existent files and never prompt. Overrides -i and -I.\"\n37\t      - R2.3:\n38\t          text: \"When -r and -f are combined, must silently remove directory trees without prompting.\"\n39\t      - R2.4:\n40\t          text: \"-d or --dir must remove empty directories. Without -d or -r, directory removal fails.\"\n41\t\n42\t  R3:\n43\t    title: Interactive modes and verbose output\n44\t    items:\n45\t      - R3.1:\n46\t          text: \"-i must prompt before every removal.\"\n47\t      - R3.2:\n48\t          text: \"-I must prompt once before removing more than three files or when removing recursively.\"\n49\t      - R3.3:\n50\t          text: \"-v or --verbose must print the name of each file as it is removed.\"\n51\t      - R3.4:\n52\t          text: \"--interactive=WHEN must control prompting. WHEN is 'never' (like -f), 'once' (like -I), or 'always' (like -i).\"\n53\t\n54\t  R4:\n55\t    title: Exit codes and differential testing\n56\t    items:\n57\t      - R4.1:\n58\t          text: Must exit 0 when all files are removed successfully.\n59\t      - R4.2:\n60\t          text: Must exit 1 when any removal fails. Must continue removing remaining files.\n61\t      - R4.3:\n62\t          text: \"With -f, must exit 0 even when specified files do not exist.\"\n63\t      - R4.4:\n64\t          text: \"Differential tests must compare exit codes and resulting file system state between the Go binary and the reference binary via pkg/testutils. Tests must cover: single file removal, multi-file removal, -r recursive, -f force on non-existent, -d empty directory, -v verbose, error on directory without -r, error on permission denied, and refusing to remove '.' or '..'.\"\n65\t\n66\tnon_goals:\n67\t  - cmd/rm does not implement --one-file-system (skip directories on different filesystems during recursive removal).\n68\t  - cmd/rm does not implement --preserve-root and --no-preserve-root. The default behavior refuses to remove root.\n69\t  - cmd/rm does not implement shred-on-delete or secure deletion.\n70\t\n71\tacceptance_criteria:\n72\t  - id: AC1\n73\t    criterion: \"touch f && go run ./cmd/rm f removes the file, matching grm.\"\n74\t    traces:\n75\t      - R1.1\n76\t      - R1.2\n77\t      - R1.3\n78\t      - R1.4\n79\t  - id: AC2\n80\t    criterion: \"mkdir -p d/sub && go run ./cmd/rm -r d removes the directory tree, matching grm.\"\n81\t    traces:\n82\t      - R1.2\n83\t      - R2.1\n84\t      - R2.3\n85\t      - R2.4\n86\t      - R4.4\n87\t  - id: AC3\n88\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/rm -f nonexistent exits 0 silently, matching grm.\"\n89\t    traces:\n90\t      - R2.2\n91\t      - R2.3\n92\t      - R3.4\n93\t      - R4.1\n94\t      - R4.2\n95\t      - R4.3\n96\t      - R4.4\n97\t  - id: AC4\n98\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/rm -v f prints the removal, matching grm.\"\n99\t    traces:\n100\t      - R3.3\n101\t      - R4.4\n102\t  - id: AC5\n103\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/rm dir without -r exits 1 with error, matching grm.\"\n104\t    traces:\n105\t      - R1.2\n106\t      - R1.3\n107\t      - R1.4\n108\t      - R2.1\n109\t      - R2.3\n110\t      - R2.4\n111\t      - R4.1\n112\t      - R4.2\n113\t      - R4.3\n114\t      - R4.4\n115\t  - id: AC6\n116\t    criterion: \"Differential test against grm passes for all flag combinations listed in R4.4.\"\n117\t    traces:\n118\t      - R4.4\n119\t  - id: AC7\n120\t    criterion: \"cmd/rm compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n121\t    traces:\n122\t      - R1.1\n123\t      - R1.2\n124\t      - R1.3\n125\t      - R1.4\n126\t      - R2.1\n127\t      - R2.2\n128\t      - R2.3\n129\t      - R2.4\n130\t      - R3.1\n131\t      - R3.2\n132\t      - R3.3\n133\t      - R3.4\n134\t      - R4.1\n135\t      - R4.2\n136\t      - R4.3\n137\t      - R4.4\n138\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a3eabc76-d363-4d82-9921-dd26e42727d9","uuid":"67bb4301-3c69-44a6-b617-e19588359948","timestamp":"2026-05-21T13:14:17.968Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5405/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd058-rm.yaml","content":"id: srd058-rm\ntitle: \"cmd/rm: Remove Files or Directories\"\n\nproblem: |\n  rm removes files and directories from the filesystem. The macOS BSD rm differs from\n  GNU rm in interactive prompt formatting, --one-file-system behavior, and verbose output.\n  The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (grm, installed by\n  coreutils) on exit codes and observable file system state for all supported flag\n  combinations, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Remove files and directories with configurable safety controls.\n  - G2: Support recursive directory removal and interactive confirmation modes.\n  - G3: Support force mode to suppress errors on non-existent files.\n  - G4: Verify functional parity against grm via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Basic file removal\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: \"When given one or more FILE arguments, must remove each file using unlink(2).\"\n      - R1.2:\n          text: \"Without -r, must refuse to remove a directory and print an error to stderr.\"\n      - R1.3:\n          text: \"Must not remove '.' or '..' to prevent accidental directory tree destruction. Must print an error if either is specified.\"\n      - R1.4:\n          text: \"When a file cannot be removed (permission denied, in use), must print an error to stderr and continue with remaining files.\"\n\n  R2:\n    title: Recursive removal and force mode\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"-r or -R or --recursive must remove directories and their contents recursively.\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: \"-f or --force must ignore non-existent files and never prompt. Overrides -i and -I.\"\n      - R2.3:\n          text: \"When -r and -f are combined, must silently remove directory trees without prompting.\"\n      - R2.4:\n          text: \"-d or --dir must remove empty directories. Without -d or -r, directory removal fails.\"\n\n  R3:\n    title: Interactive modes and verbose output\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: \"-i must prompt before every removal.\"\n      - R3.2:\n          text: \"-I must prompt once before removing more than three files or when removing recursively.\"\n      - R3.3:\n          text: \"-v or --verbose must print the name of each file as it is removed.\"\n      - R3.4:\n          text: \"--interactive=WHEN must control prompting. WHEN is 'never' (like -f), 'once' (like -I), or 'always' (like -i).\"\n\n  R4:\n    title: Exit codes and differential testing\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 when all files are removed successfully.\n      - R4.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 when any removal fails. Must continue removing remaining files.\n      - R4.3:\n          text: \"With -f, must exit 0 even when specified files do not exist.\"\n      - R4.4:\n          text: \"Differential tests must compare exit codes and resulting file system state between the Go binary and the reference binary via pkg/testutils. Tests must cover: single file removal, multi-file removal, -r recursive, -f force on non-existent, -d empty directory, -v verbose, error on directory without -r, error on permission denied, and refusing to remove '.' or '..'.\"\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/rm does not implement --one-file-system (skip directories on different filesystems during recursive removal).\n  - cmd/rm does not implement --preserve-root and --no-preserve-root. The default behavior refuses to remove root.\n  - cmd/rm does not implement shred-on-delete or secure deletion.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"touch f && go run ./cmd/rm f removes the file, matching grm.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"mkdir -p d/sub && go run ./cmd/rm -r d removes the directory tree, matching grm.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.2\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n      - R4.4\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/rm -f nonexistent exits 0 silently, matching grm.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.4\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n      - R4.4\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/rm -v f prints the removal, matching grm.\"\n    traces:\n      - R3.3\n      - R4.4\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/rm dir without -r exits 1 with error, matching grm.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n      - R4.4\n  - id: AC6\n    criterion: \"Differential test against grm passes for all flag combinations listed in R4.4.\"\n    traces:\n      - R4.4\n  - id: AC7\n    criterion: \"cmd/rm compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n      - R3.4\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n      - R4.4\n","numLines":138,"startLine":1,"totalLines":138}}}
