{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (cobbler orchestrator) assigned stitch task #5405 to implement srd058-rm requirements R3.1-R3.4 (interactive modes and verbose output) in cmd/rm. Specifically:\n   - R3.1: `-i` must prompt before every removal\n   - R3.2: `-I` must prompt once before removing more than three files or when removing recursively\n   - R3.3: `-v` or `--verbose` must print the name of each file as it is removed\n   - R3.4: `--interactive=WHEN` must control prompting (never/once/always)\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/rm/main.go` and `cmd/rm/rm_test.go`. Must pass `go build`, `go vet`, and `go test` including differential tests against `grm`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary against GNU `grm`\n   - Interactive prompting via stderr output and stdin reading (GNU rm prompts on stderr, reads y/n from stdin)\n   - `interactiveMode` enum type already defined: `interactiveNever`, `interactiveOnce`, `interactiveAlways`\n   - SIGPIPE handler required via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - `LC_ALL=C` environment for deterministic test output\n   - DiffTest struct has `Stdin []byte` field for providing stdin input to interactive tests\n   - Binary name normalization in tests via regex replacing `grm`/`rm` paths\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd058-rm.yaml`\n     - Source of truth for requirements R3.1-R3.4\n     - R3.1: `-i` prompt before every removal\n     - R3.2: `-I` prompt once before >3 files or recursive\n     - R3.3: `-v`/`--verbose` print each removed file\n     - R3.4: `--interactive=WHEN` with never/once/always values\n     - Non-goals: no --one-file-system, no --preserve-root, no secure deletion\n\n   - `cmd/rm/main.go` (existing, needs modification)\n     - Already has `interactiveMode` type with three values and `options` struct with all relevant fields\n     - `parseFlags` already handles `-i`, `-I`, `-v`, `--interactive=WHEN`, `--verbose`\n     - `stdinScanner = bufio.NewScanner(os.Stdin)` declared but unused\n     - `promptRemoval(path string, isDir bool) bool` is a STUB returning false - needs real implementation\n     - `shouldPromptOnce(paths []string, opts options) bool` is a STUB returning false - needs real implementation\n     - `removeFile`, `removeDir`, `removeEmptyDir` already print verbose output but do NOT check interactive mode before removing\n     - `removePath` and `removeFiles` do not wire up interactive prompting\n     - Key code patterns: errors formatted as `rm: cannot remove 'X': msg`, verbose output as `removed 'X'` or `removed directory 'X'`\n\n   - `cmd/rm/rm_test.go` (existing, needs modification)\n     - Has `TestDiff` with many subtests for R1-R2 requirements\n     - Uses custom `runRemovalTest`, `runBin`, `compareResults` helpers (not the standard RunDiffTests for most tests)\n     - `runBin` sets `LC_ALL=C`, uses 10s timeout, captures stdout/stderr/exitCode\n     - `normalizeBinaryName` replaces binary name paths with \"rm\" for comparison\n     - Already has verbose tests: `verbose_single_file`, `verbose_recursive`\n     - Needs new tests for `-i`, `-I`, and `--interactive=WHEN` modes\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Was in reading/planning phase when summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that R3.3 (verbose) is already partially implemented - the flag parsing and output in `removeFile`/`removeEmptyDir` already exist, and test cases already exist\n   - Identified two stub functions (`promptRemoval`, `shouldPromptOnce`) that need real implementation\n   - Identified that interactive prompting needs to be wired into the removal flow (check before each removal for `-i`, check once at start for `-I`)\n   - For GNU rm compatibility: prompts go to stderr, format is `rm: remove regular file 'X'?` or `rm: remove directory 'X'?`, reads y/Y/yes responses\n   - For `-I` mode: GNU rm prompts `rm: remove N arguments?` when >3 files, or `rm: remove N arguments recursively?` when recursive\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The full stitch task prompt with massive project context, SRD specifications, execution constitution, coding standards, and specific task description for implementing srd058-rm R3.1-R3.4\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - Instructions to provide a summary only without tool usage.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Implement `promptRemoval()` function to actually prompt user and read y/n response from stdin\n   - Implement `shouldPromptOnce()` to check >3 files or recursive removal\n   - Wire interactive mode checks into `removeFiles()` (for -I once check) and `removePath()`/`removeFile()`/`removeDir()`/`removeEmptyDir()` (for -i always check)\n   - Add differential test cases for -i, -I, and --interactive=WHEN modes in rm_test.go\n   - Run `go build -o bin/rm ./cmd/rm/`, `go vet ./cmd/rm/`, and `go test ./cmd/rm/ -count=1`\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the three required files (srd058-rm.yaml, cmd/rm/main.go, cmd/rm/rm_test.go) and was about to begin implementing the changes. The planning phase was complete:\n   \n   - `promptRemoval` needs to prompt on stderr with format matching GNU rm (e.g., `rm: remove regular file 'X'? `) and read y/Y/yes from stdin using the existing `stdinScanner`\n   - `shouldPromptOnce` needs to return true when `opts.interactive == interactiveOnce` and either `len(paths) > 3` or `opts.recursive` is true\n   - `removeFiles` needs to call `shouldPromptOnce` and abort if user says no\n   - `removeFile`, `removeEmptyDir`, and `removeDir` need to check `opts.interactive == interactiveAlways` and call `promptRemoval` before proceeding